Integrated product designs where wear and degradation spread throughout material matrices create complexity and inefficiency during remanufacturing. Layered architectures concentrate degradation in outer sacrificial layers while preserving high-value cores. This stratification enables selective component replacement and efficient material recovery.

Layer-based designs create conditions for specialized remanufacturing processes optimized for each layer type. Surface cleaning processes can be harsh without damaging durable cores. Architectural separation enables parallel processing of different layers by specialized equipment.